{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>משוד.</b> Like ושוד מלכים תינקי (Isaiah 60:16). The meaning is: abundance of joys, for consolation is the opposite of mourning." "<b>תמוצו.</b> Like מיץ חלב (Proverbs 30:33). And if they are two roots." "<b>מזיז כבודה.</b> Jonathan ben Uzziel said: חמד. Rabbi Moses the Cohen said: like וזיז שדי (Psalms 50:11), and it is somewhat far-fetched. The correct interpretation is that it has no [other] meaning."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:13.283726324Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}